  "findings": [
    {
      "finding_id": "F1-EVIDENCE-RECEIPT-STATUS-DURATION-CONTRACT-UNDERBOUND",
      "severity": "HIGH",
      "status": "BLOCKER",
      "title": "The corrected receipt contract still cannot represent or validate the required real command duration/status/exit failure domain",
      "requirements": [
        "Review directive: closure of the predecessor HIGH requires exact command inventory plus real test_count/pass/fail/skip/duration/status/exit coherence and forbids synthetic counts.",
        "Ratified D0-13 lines 1580-1586 require the qualification-receipt schema to carry the command list with exit/result/test/pass/fail/skip counts, start/end timestamps, and terminal PASS|FAIL.",
        "Ratified D0-15 line 1686 requires corrected evidence and an entirely new terminal-green run/artifact set for an evidence/count mismatch."
      ],
      "affected_surfaces": [
        "contracts/identity/GKOS-AGENT-IDENTITY-MCP-CONTRACT-1.0.0-draft.1/qualification-receipt.schema.json 5073 bytes sha256:3c459b901854758ac187de5141672e854580151ec5feada437f29a0540995d59",
        "scripts/generate-agent-identity-mcp-contract.mjs 91925 bytes sha256:7229c774ed1fc96188538f7d6e6a6114b25a00d4f16a81cb5696d1980ca5f8ab",
        "test/agent-identity-mcp-contract.test.mjs 13861 bytes sha256:6afd8b9c4761202f06d12392b933a0a59824888811cc7f7ad314c0da000f8bff",
        ".github/workflows/phase6-identity-contract.yml 28238 bytes sha256:927c9b832dee98383f020e4607a02b77783aa6c85e1004c10c7677243600361b"
      ],
      "observations": [
        "The command object requires command, exit_code, result, test_count, pass_count, fail_count, and skip_count, but has no duration field; additionalProperties:false makes a duration field invalid.",
        "All 11 hosted receipts contain zero command-duration fields. Their started_at/ended_at intervals are only 71-290 ms and measure receipt generation after the commands, not command execution. The Linux24 full TAP alone records 575924.402944 ms while its receipt interval is 76 ms.",
        "An independently mutated receipt with incoherent test_count arithmetic still validates against the strict schema. The focused test at line 66 explicitly asserts that schema validation succeeds for this synthetic mutation and then relies on out-of-schema generator/terminal logic to notice it.",
        "The receipt schema hard-codes top-level result=PASS, command result=PASS, exit_code=0, and fail_count=0. It rejects terminal FAIL and any failed command status/exit, contrary to the ratified PASS|FAIL receipt domain.",
        "Non-test commands are supplied after execution as free --receipt-command strings and are emitted as synthetic PASS/0 records; no per-command durable log, duration, or captured exit record binds those assertions. Hosted job success independently shows this run passed, but does not repair the underbound receipt contract."
      ],
      "why_green_does_not_close": "The real TAP bytes and exact test counts reconcile and the terminal auditor enforces arithmetic for this run, but the versioned strict receipt schema and every retained receipt still omit/reject duration and failure evidence and accept an incoherent count mutation. The exact prior HIGH closure requested schema-level durable evidence, not only a green post-hoc terminal invariant.",
      "required_disposition": "REJECT / F1_NO_GO. Align the versioned receipt contract and produced receipts with the ratified duration/status/exit and PASS|FAIL domain, make incoherent counts invalid under the authoritative validation contract, and produce an entirely new 11/11 terminal-green run/artifact set for fresh independent review."
    },
    {
